From 3ac18161a2d9f063451db041dd36e6be17c4062d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 23:05:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] discovery: Iraq seed gains igs's spellings
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

igs now loads this seed (configs/discovery/iraq.yaml, copied unchanged)
and kept the spellings its discovery matched that the seed lacked in
its own additions file. This adds them here, so the two lists are one:

- iraq: Irak, Iraqis, Iraqia; عيراق
- kurdistan_region: Kurdistan, كردستان, كوردستان, کوردستان, Kurdistanê
  (Kurdistan alone also names the Kurdish parts of Turkey, Syria and
  Iran; turn it off in the table if its searches bring in mostly pages
  from outside Iraq)
- erbil: هولير
- sulaymaniyah: Sulaymani; سليماني off (also a common surname)
- anbar: انبار
- babil: حلة off (also "outfit", "a new look")
- dhi_qar: Dhiqar, ذيقار
- maysan: Misan

Loading the seed again (fbctl discovery keywords seed) adds only these;
keywords already listed keep their state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01E488KDjGFuWptvrd8QU5Bf
---
 configs/discovery/iraq.yaml | 31 +++++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configs/discovery/iraq.yaml b/configs/discovery/iraq.yaml
index af81259..5855f2c 100644
